        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12390451/comment/12577798",
          "id": "12577798",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=mreutegg&avatarId=18658"
            },
            "displayName": "Marcel Reutegger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "So far I haven't been able to reproduce the deadlock with a test.\n\nJust looking at the thread dump we can avoid the deadlock by pulling the getPath() in LockManagerImpl.getLockInfo() out of the acquire/release() scope.\n\nI've attached a patch with that change.\n\nPrzemo, can you please build jackrabbit-core-1.3.4-rc1 again with this patch applied and check if the deadlock still occurs?\n\nIt also seems that there's another thread involved in the deadlock. Can you please attach the complete thread dump? Stripping off application specific stack frames is of course OK.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
